WEBVTT

00:42:26.292 --> 00:42:30.208
And I think I've just taken for granted
that people know that's true.

00:42:31.458 --> 00:42:33.268
EP: You know, I was raised like that.

00:42:33.292 --> 00:42:36.268
This was pretty much
much more of a cultural norm growing up.

00:42:36.292 --> 00:42:37.934
AG: This explains it a lot.

00:42:37.958 --> 00:42:39.101
(Laughter)

00:42:39.125 --> 00:42:42.434
EP: I mean, it's like,
we were not praised as much,

00:42:42.458 --> 00:42:46.684
you were not pumped up
and you had to learn the distinction

00:42:46.708 --> 00:42:51.559
between this is not good
versus you are not good.

00:42:51.583 --> 00:42:54.309
And it was not an easy thing to learn.

00:42:54.333 --> 00:42:58.059
AG: That is the fundamental distinction
in psychology between guilt and shame.

00:42:58.083 --> 00:42:59.851
EP: Yes. Correct, correct.

00:42:59.875 --> 00:43:02.768
But it is very much the educational model